00:48:33.000 --> 00:49:12.000
Ivy denied ever having a sexual relationship with Helen, stating, That amazes me that anyone's ever said that. I can't think of any situation that I've ever been in where someone would think something like that. Ivy said his memories of Russell were limited, and that he couldn't recall whether he spoke to Helen about his disappearance. He also claimed not to know whether there was any domestic violence in their marriage. But when pushed, he said, Well, from my recollection, they did have a fiery type of marriage. They were a fiery couple.
伊维否认曾与海伦有过性关系，并表示：“这让我感到震惊，居然有人会说出这种话。我想象不出我曾身处任何会让别人产生这种想法的境地。”伊维说他对罗素的记忆很有限，并且不记得自己是否曾向海伦提及他的失踪。他还声称不知道他们的婚姻中是否存在家庭暴力。但在追问之下，他说道：“嗯，据我回忆，他们确实有过一段激烈的婚姻。他们是一对火爆的夫妻。”

50
00:49:12.000 --> 00:50:18.000
It was Russell's sister Bev and mother Ellen who had filed the official missing persons report to senior constable Kennedy in 1977. A second missing persons report was tended in court that appeared to have been filed later by Helen and signed by Peter Ivy. Ivy said he didn't take the report, but couldn't explain why his name was on it. Helen was spoken to after Bev and Ellen made their initial report. No one was able to explain to the court why this second report was signed with Peter Ivy's name. Russell's youngest son, Paul, testified that he had recently been approached by a man who claimed to know where his father's body was. The man had taken him to the location the night before, but Paul had been unable to find it when he returned to the side on his own in the morning.
正是罗素的姐姐贝夫和母亲埃伦在1977年向资深警员肯尼迪提交了正式的失踪人口报告。法庭上出示了一份第二份失踪人口报告，这份报告似乎是后来由海伦提交并由彼得·伊维签署的。伊维说他没有受理该报告，但无法解释为什么上面会有他的名字。在贝夫和埃伦提交最初的报告后，警方找海伦谈过话。没有人能向法庭解释为什么这份第二份报告上会签署彼得·伊维的名字。罗素的小儿子保罗作证说，他最近被一个声称知道他父亲尸体在哪里的男人接近了。那个男人在前一天晚上带他去了那个地点，但当保罗早上独自一人返回该地点时，他没能找到。

51
00:50:18.000 --> 00:51:15.000
He refused to name the man as he didn't want to get him in trouble. Paul said he would show the police the location once he had verified it during the daylight. Based on this tip-off, the court heard that members of the state emergency service attended an area at Green Lake. The off-stream reservoir and recreational area was 55 kilometres northwest of the store. There, they located two sunken areas in the ground. They dug approximately one foot deep, but found no indication that anything was buried there. Over the years, suspicion had also been cast on Helen's new husband, Charles Smith. Charles testified that sitting in court was the first time he had ever heard that anyone thought Helen had something to do with it.
他拒绝说出这个男人的名字，因为他不想给他惹麻烦。保罗说，一旦他在白天核实了地点，他就会把位置指给警察看。根据这条线索，法庭得知州紧急服务部门的人员前往了绿湖附近的一个地区。这个离槽水库和娱乐区位于斯托尔西北55公里处。在那里，他们找到了地面上的两个下沉区域。他们向下挖了大约一英尺深，但没有发现任何东西被埋在那里的迹象。这些年来，海伦的新丈夫查尔斯·史密斯也受到了怀疑。查尔斯作证说，坐在法庭里是他第一次听说有人认为海伦与此事有关。

52
00:51:15.000 --> 00:52:07.000
He said he'd heard all kinds of rumours over the years, but never had any interest in delving into them further. He denied having ever met Russell and asserted that he had met Helen for the first time years after her husband's disappearance. This contradicted a statement made by Charles and Russell's mutual friend, Alan Frame. Alan said the men lived close to one another, moved in the same social circles, and had known each other from the pub. He considered it unlikely that they had never crossed paths. Helen appeared on the stand. She was asked whether she was concerned that Russell might return home to find she had moved on with another man. Helen responded,
他说他这些年来听过各种各样的传言，但从没有兴趣去进一步深究。他否认自己曾见过罗素，并坚称他在海伦丈夫失踪多年后才第一次见到海伦。这与查尔斯和罗素的共同朋友阿兰·弗雷姆的陈述相矛盾。阿兰说，这两个男人住得很近，在同一个社交圈活动，并且在酒吧里就认识对方。他认为他们从未擦肩而过的可能性微乎其微。海伦出庭作证。她被问及是否担心罗素可能会回家发现她已经和另一个男人开始了新生活。海伦回答说，

53
00:52:07.000 --> 00:53:16.000
I was always concerned about him returning, yes, but I had to live my own life too. She denied having any involvement in or knowledge of any foul play against Russell. She said that she had provided police with the number plate details of the car she thought Russell had left in. Officers had no record of this information and suspected she was lying. Detective Mark McCann, who had taken over as lead detective on the case, told the court, I believe that Russell Martin has been murdered and I further believe that Helen Smith has more knowledge of it than she has led the court to believe thus far. On July 5 2002, Coroner Timothy McDonald handed down his findings. He deemed the evidence given by Helen, her husband Charles Smith, and former stall police officer Peter Ivey to be unconvincing and evasive.
“我一直担心他会回来，是的，但我也不得不过我自己的生活。”她否认自己参与或知晓针对罗素的任何不法行为。她说她已经向警方提供了她认为罗素离开时所坐的那辆车的车牌详情。警官们没有这条信息的记录，并怀疑她在撒谎。作为该案首席侦探的侦探马克·麦坎对法庭表示：“我相信罗素·马丁已经被谋杀，并且我进一步相信，海伦·史密斯对该案的了解比她目前向法庭透露的要多。”2002年7月5日，验尸官蒂莫西·麦克唐纳宣布了他的调查结果。他认为海伦、她的丈夫查尔斯·史密斯以及前斯托尔警官彼得·伊维的证词缺乏说服力且闪烁其词。

54
00:53:16.000 --> 00:54:22.000
Quote, I am satisfied that the witness Peter Ivey was not a frank, open, or truthful witness in the evidence that he gave to the court. I did not accept that a person who was a police officer and who played sport with Russell Martin and drove his truck to assist him when he had a broken ankle would have such little memory of the details surrounding Martin going missing. He was an unreliable witness. Further, I am satisfied that Charles Smith knows more of the circumstances surrounding the disappearance of Russell Martin than what he has told investigators in this court. He was an evasive and vague witness who was hard to pin down to give clear and definitive evidence. Smith has indicated to investigators that he had little or no knowledge of Russell Martin at the time of his disappearance. He says he may have met him at a hotel at some time, but cannot recall this.
原话是，“我确信证人彼得·伊维在向法庭提供的证词中不是一个坦率、公开或真实的证人。我不接受一个曾担任警官、和罗素·马丁一起进行体育运动并在他脚踝骨折时开车去协助他的这样一个对马丁失踪的细节几乎毫无记忆的人。他是一个不可靠的证人。此外，我确信查尔斯·史密斯对罗素·马丁失踪的周围情况的了解比他在本法庭上向调查人员所说的要多。他是一个闪烁其词、含糊不清的证人，很难让他给出清晰明确的证词。史密斯曾向调查人员表示，他在罗素·马丁失踪时对其实际上一无所知或知之甚少。他说他可能曾在某个时候在酒店见过他，但对此记不清了。”

55
00:54:22.000 --> 00:55:39.000
This is inconsistent with the evidence of Alan Frayne. Because of the unreliability of Smith's evidence, I am unable to accept his assertion that he was not known to Helen Martin prior to the 20th of January 1977. Helen Smith has also been vague, unclear, and misleading in what she has told different people about the circumstances of her husband's disappearance. What I am satisfied of is that the behavior of Helen Martin, very shortly after she says her husband left home, is consistent with her knowing that he would never return. Other than saying that her husband told her he would not be returning, there is no evidence before this inquest for the court to find that it would be reasonable for Helen Martin to believe that this would be the case. Reasons for reaching this conclusion are the evidence before the court is that Russell Martin loved his children. He had strong family and other ties in store. Whenever he had left the matrimonial home on other occasions, he had always returned.
这与阿兰·弗雷姆的证词不一致。由于史密斯证词的不可靠性，我无法接受他关于自己在1977年1月20日之前不认识海伦·马丁的断言。海伦·史密斯在向不同的人讲述她丈夫失踪的情况时，也一直含糊不清、模棱两可且具有误导性。我所确信的是，海伦·马丁在她声称丈夫离开家后不久的行为，与她知道他绝不会回来的情况是一致的。除了说她的丈夫告诉她他不会回来之外，本次研讯中没有任何证据能让法庭认定海伦·马丁认为会是这种情况是合理的。得出这一结论的理由是，法庭掌握的证据表明罗素·马丁深爱他的孩子。他在斯托尔拥有牢固的家庭和其他纽带。每当他在其他场合离开婚姻住所时，他总是会回来的。

56
00:55:39.000 --> 00:56:42.000
Witnesses have given evidence that he would not leave store without ever having some contact with the people he loved. There is no reasonable explanation before the court as to why he would want to leave store permanently. Coroner McDonald believed the information provided by Russell's now deceased neighbour, Charlie Stanhouse. Charlie said he had visited the Martin House on Wednesday, January 19 and saw Russell bedridden and in a delirious state. Coroner McDonald quote, I am satisfied that Helen Smith has not disclosed the true circumstances surrounding the disappearance of her husband to the court. Further, I'm satisfied that she possesses information that is likely to establish such circumstances. After taking into account all of the evidence before the court,
证人们作证说，他绝不会在没有与他所爱的人进行某种联系的情况下离开斯托尔。法庭面前没有任何合理的解释能够说明他为什么要永久离开斯托尔。麦克唐纳验尸官相信了罗素现已去世的邻居查理·斯坦豪斯提供的信息。查理说他曾在1月19日星期三访问过马丁家，并看到罗素卧床不起且处于神志不清的状态。麦克唐纳验尸官原话：“我确信海伦·史密斯没有向法庭透露她丈夫失踪的真实情况。此外，我确信她掌握着很可能证实这种真实情况的信息。”在考虑了法庭上的所有证据之后，

57
00:56:42.000 --> 00:57:56.000
I'm satisfied that the disappearance of Russell Martin on or about the 20th of January 1977 was associated with suspicious circumstances and that he died on or about that date from causes that were not natural. Despite these findings, there was no new information that warranted Russell's case being reinvestigated and no arrests were made. Russell's sister Bev was pleased with the coroner's findings but disappointed that no further inquiries would take place. She provided a DNA sample to the Victorian Institute of Forensic Medicine to be compared with their collection of unidentified human remains. There wasn't a match. She tried every available avenue to have Russell's case heard or reinvestigated and meticulously noted, filed and reported every new lead that came her way. A person can only apply to the coroner to have the case reopened if there is substantial new information available.
我确信罗素·马丁在1977年1月20日左右的失踪与可疑情况有关，并且他在该日或前后死于非自然原因。尽管有这些发现，但并没有出现足以让罗素的案件被重新调查的新信息，也没有人被捕。罗素的姐姐贝夫对验尸官的调查结果感到满意，但对不会进行进一步调查感到失望。她向维多利亚法医学研究所提供了DNA样本，以便与他们的未名人类遗骸收藏进行比对。没有找到匹配的。她尝试了所有可用的途径来让罗素的案件得到审理或重新调查，并一丝不苟地记录、存档和举报了她遇到的每一个新线索。一个人只有在有大量新信息可用的情况下，才能向验尸官申请重审此案。

58
00:57:56.000 --> 00:59:05.000
Bev has tried several times over the years to have Russell's case reopened. Recently, a local man came forward claiming to have seen Russell put into a police van by a known local officer, never to be seen again. However, this claim didn't match with the timing of information known to be true, such as Russell's last doctor's appointment. In March 2020, Bev received a letter from the coroner's court saying they couldn't take the matter any further and that, quote, These inquiries have now been exhausted and therefore the police investigation is currently considered inactive. Most people want Bev to move on, due in part to Russell's history of violence and crime. Some may think Russell deserved his outcome, whatever it may have been. Bev accepts that her brother was no angel, but believes that justice should prevail.
这些年来，贝夫曾多次试图让罗素的案件重新开庭。最近，当地一名男子站出来声称，曾看到罗素被一名当地的知名警官推上一辆警车，从此再也没有露面。然而，这一说法与已知真实信息的时机不符，例如罗素最近一次看医生的预约。2020年3月，贝夫收到验尸官法院的一封信，称他们无法将此事进一步推进，并且原话是，“这些调查现已用尽，因此警方目前认为该调查处于不活跃状态。”大多数人都希望贝夫向前看，部分原因是因为罗素有暴力和犯罪的历史。有些人可能认为罗素无论遭遇了什么都是罪有应得。贝夫承认她的弟弟并非天使，但她坚信正义应当战胜一切。

59
00:59:05.000 --> 00:59:10.000
Judging victims of crime based on their character and only investigating the murders of those who are deemed to good is not what the law is about. Bev is getting on in years and her health is beginning to fail her. Russell's brothers have passed away and she feels that she is the only one left who cares that he's gone. All she wants before she joins her brothers is to get some sort of resolution. For over two decades, Bev has written to police chiefs, lawyers, magistrates, coroners and to the missing persons advocacy network. She has begged them all for the same thing. Please find out what happened to my brother, Russell. You There aren't comments yet for this episode. Click on any sentence in the transcript to leave a comment.
根据犯罪受害者的品格来对他们进行评判，并且只调查那些被认为足够好的人的谋杀案，这并非法律的初衷。贝夫已经上了年纪，她的健康状况也开始恶化。罗素的兄弟们已经去世，她觉得她是唯一一个还在乎他已经离去的人。在她与她的兄弟们团聚之前，她所渴望的只是获得某种结果。二十多年来，贝夫一直写信给警察局长、律师、地方法官、验尸官以及失踪人口倡导网络。她向他们所有人乞求同一件事。请查明我弟弟罗素身上究竟发生了什么。本集目前还没有评论。点击剧本中的任意句子即可留下评论。
